_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 27
---
order: 27
---
short_label: IX.27
---
statement: If an even number is subtracted from an odd number, then the remainder is odd.
---
proof:

Let the even number *BC* be subtracted from the odd number *AB.*

I say that the remainder *CA* is odd.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="230" height="60" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="IX.27 diagram" src="propIX27.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "IX.27",
        elements: [
            "A0;point;free;-1000,30;0;0",
            "A3;point;free;1000,30;0;0",
            "U1;point;free;1000,0;0;0",
            "U2;point;free;1000,20;0;0",
            "A;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,30,0",
            "B;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,200,0",
            "C;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,130,0",
            "D;point;cutoff;A,B,U1,U2",
            "AB;line;connect;A,B"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

Subtract the unit *AD,* therefore *DB* is even. [!just VII.Def.7]

But *BC* is also even, therefore the remainder *CD* is even. Therefore *CA* is odd. [!just IX.24, VII.Def.7]

Therefore, *if an even number is subtracted from an odd number, then the remainder is odd.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
---
body:

This is the last of four propositions that examine the result of subtracting even and odd numbers from each other.
